class Solution {
public:
    int hammingWeight(uint32_t n) {
        int count = 0;

        while (n) {
            n = n & (n - 1);
            count++;
        }

        return count;
    }
};
**Intuition:**  
Use `n & (n - 1)` to remove the rightmost set bit (1).  
Count how many times this operation can be performed.

**Algorithm:**  
Keep applying `n = n & (n - 1)` until `n` becomes 0.  
Each operation removes one `1` bit, so the count gives the answer.

**Complexity:**  
Time: **O(k)**  
Space: **O(1)**
